WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.620
Two tubes: a blue
solution and a green one.

2
00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:06.760
Add a few drops of sodium
hydroxide to each.

3
00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:12.160
In both, a solid appears: pale blue
in one, dull green in the other.

4
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.240
Keep adding.

5
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.580
The pale blue solid just sits there.

6
00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:20.620
But the dull green solid vanishes,
leaving a clear, dark green solution.

7
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:26.130
So why does extra alkali make some precipitates
vanish, but leave others untouched?

8
00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:31.640
In this mission, you'll identify metal ions
from the shade of the precipitate they form.

9
00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:34.840
Then you'll build a chart
of tests, step by step,

10
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:38.040
that can name the ion
in an unknown solution.

11
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:43.310
Your mission: explain why extra alkali
dissolves some precipitates but not others.